# DTF tier manifest: nuget-cred-scoping  (issue #2925)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mocknuget (two stdlib http
# servers on the slot's private 172.16/12 subnet: `mock-nuget-index` = the
# configured upstream, `mock-nuget-foreign` = the other host its service index
# names; both log the Authorization header of every request; health-gated
# instantly).
#
# WHAT THIS DISCRIMINATES (#2925): a NuGet V3 remote proxy discovers its
# RegistrationsBaseUrl / PackageBaseAddress resource bases from the upstream
# *service index response*, then fetches from those bases carrying the repo's
# configured upstream credentials (`apply_upstream_auth`, keyed by repo). A
# malicious or compromised upstream service index can name an attacker host in
# those resources, causing the proxy to send the configured credentials there
# (credential exfiltration / SSRF-adjacent). The fix
# (backend/src/api/handlers/nuget.rs `guard_upstream_base` + `same_upstream_origin`)
# refuses any discovered base whose host+effective-port differs from the
# configured `upstream_url` origin, with a 502, BEFORE any credentialed fetch.
#
# The oracle stands up two mock hosts, configures TWO remote nuget repos (both
# with the same Basic upstream credentials):
#   * nuget-foreign : upstream_url -> mock-nuget-index/foreign/index.json, whose
#                     service index points the flat-container base at the FOREIGN
#                     host (the exploit)
#   * nuget-samehost: upstream_url -> mock-nuget-index/samehost/index.json, whose
#                     service index points the base back at the index host itself
#                     (the legitimate case)
# then drives `GET /nuget/<repo>/v3/flatcontainer/testpkg/index.json` on each and
# asserts:
#   N1  the FOREIGN host received NO credentialed request (no `AUTH=Basic` line):
#       the configured credentials were never sent off the configured host
#   N2  AK REFUSED the off-host resolution with HTTP 502 (before any credentialed
#       fetch), not 200
#   N3  regression: the SAME-host resource still gets the credentials (index host
#       logs a credentialed `/sh-flat/` request) and AK returns 200 -- the fix
#       does not break legitimate same-host proxying
# NON-ZERO-WHILE-BUG: pre-#2925 the foreign host receives `AUTH=Basic ...` and AK
# returns 200, so N1 and N2 fail; only the fixed image exits 0. N3 passes on both
# images and guards the fix against over-blocking.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives admin login + repo creates +
# proxy fetches back-to-back through one admin user (relax a shipped control
# explicitly; base default stays ON).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mocknuget"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
